=============================================================
Detection: System binary process execution, process creation & network connection data used.
Technique: T1218.005 .010 .011- MSHTA, rundll, regsvr32 combined into one hollistic rule
Tactic:    Defence evasion
Platform:  Splunk SPL. Counterpart to rule.yml (Sigma base).
Data:      XmlWinEventLog/sysmon: EventID = 1/3
Author:    William Richardson   Date: 2026-07-16  (V2)

 Description- Detects three sub-techniques of T1218 System Binary Proxy Execution:
  Mshta (T1218.005), Regsvr32 (T1218.010) and Rundll32 (T1218.011).
  These trusted, signed system binaries are abused to proxy the execution of
  malicious code past application control and signature-based defences.
  The rule looks for suspicious command-line arguments, suspicious parent/child
  process relationships, and well-known abuse patterns such as comsvcs.dll
  MiniDump credential dumping and the regsvr32 "Squiblydoo" remote scriptlet.
  Intended to be correlated with the companion network_connection rule below
  into a single KQL rule (rule.kql) with risk scoring.

OUT OF SCOPE: Detecting child process execution, an attacker could bypass 
this detection by launching a child process to act out their malicious behaviour.

ASSUMES Splunk_TA_windows auto-extracts ScriptBlockText / ScriptBlockId /
ProcessID / MessageNumber. If ScriptBlockText is empty, the TA isn't extracting -
add a rex fallback on _raw.

REGEX ESCAPING: if a match() returns nothing, your Splunk version wants doubled
backslashes - replace \. with \\. , \b with \\b , \( with \\( etc. #1 SPL gotcha.

Comment syntax (triple-backtick) needs Splunk 8.1+. Strip comments if older.
=============================================================```
index=sysmon (EventCode=1 OR EventCode=3)
 (Image="*\\mshta.exe" OR Image="*\\rundll32.exe" OR Image="*\\regsvr32.exe"
     OR OriginalFileName IN ("MSHTA.EXE","RUNDLL32.EXE","REGSVR32.EXE"))
| stats values(EventCode) as events values(CommandLine) as cmdline
        values(ParentImage) as parent values(Image) as image
        values(User) as user values(ParentProcessGuid) as parent_guid
        values(DestinationIp) as dst_ip values(DestinationPort) as dst_port
        values(DestinationHostname) as dst_host min(_time) as start
        by ProcessGuid, Computer
| eval has_network = if(match(mvjoin(events,","),"3"),1,0)


``` --- SIGNALS ------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` rundll32 ```
eval hasRundllScriptAbuse = if(match(<fieldName>, "(?i)()"),1,0)
eval hassuspRundllParent = if(match(<field name>, "(?i)()"),1,0)
eval hasCredDump = if(match(<fieldName>, "(?i)comsvcs(\.dll)?\s*,\s*(#\+?24|minidump)")1,0)
eval hasObfusc = if(match(<fieldName>), "(?i)()"),1,0)

```mshta.exe```
eval hasMshtaParentImg = if(match(<fieldName>, "(?i)()"),1,0)
eval hasMshtaChild = if(match(<FieldName>, "(?i)())"), 1,0)
eval hasMshtaCli = if(match(<fieldName>, "()"), 1,0 )
rex "fieldName= ?<GuidPresent>\{[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}\}"
then if this isnt null its suspicious?^

``` regsvr32 ```
eval hasRegsvrParent = if(match(<fieldName, "(?i)(signal)"),1,0)
eval hasSquiblydoo = if(match(<fieldName>, "(?i)(signal)"),1,0)


``` --- collapse one execution's many script blocks into ONE row (host + process) ---
    aggregate each flag via max(): 1 if ANY block in the execution carried the signal.
    This will help correlate network traffic directly to the pid that initiated it. ```
| bin _time span=10m
| stats summary function(column) AS <Renamed column or same name>
        summer function 2(column) as etc......
        by host, pid, _time <CONFIRM FIELD NAMES>




``` --- severity --- ```
| eval SeverityRank = case(
       condition 1 and condition 2),3, (condition 2 and 3), 3,
       condition 1, 2 and so on
        true(), 1)

``` --- analyst-facing reason (first match wins -> highest / most-specific first) --- ```
| eval DetectionReason = case(
        has-value , "what this means"
        true())

| eval Severity = case(SeverityRank=3, "High", SeverityRank=2, "Medium", true(), "Informational")
| where SeverityRank >= 2

``` surface every flag so the analyst sees exactly what fired ```
| table  <Enter fields>
| sort - StartTime


```
falsepositives:
All - Out of scope issue -> If one of reg/rundll/mshta spawns a child process and that process is malicious this detection wouldnt pick it up.
This is as it would overlap with a T1059.001 rule for malicious parent processes that will actually correlate parents/ grandparents etc.
  # regsvr32.exe
  - Legitimate COM/DLL registration by installers launched from script hosts (local file path, no /i URL)
  # mshta.exe
  - Legacy internal HTA-based admin tools and line-of-business applications
  # rundll32.exe
  - Installers running INF install sections via advpack.dll/setupapi.dll LaunchINFSection
  - Software updaters invoking vendor DLLs staged in %TEMP% or %APPDATA%
level: High
```